{"name":"Curious Chipmunk","hex":"#dabfa4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"curious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to ask questions, or to want to explore or investigate; inquisitive;  nosy, prying.","Caused by curiosity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or pertaining to trivalent curium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curious"},{"term":"chipmunk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain the small, striped rodents, all found in North America, with the exception of the Siberian chipmunk, placed in the taxonomic subtribe Tamiina."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speed up (an audio recording, especially a song), to make the voices high-pitched.","To fill (one's mouth or cheeks) with food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chipmunk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chipmunk","blocks":[{"text":"Chipmunks are small, striped burrowing squirrels of subtribe Tamiina. Chipmunks are found in North America, with the exception of the Siberian chipmunk, which is found primarily in Asia. The name \"chipmunk\" originated in the 19th century, and other names for this group of squirrels include chitmunk, chipmuck, chipping squirrel, and ground squirrel, though the last name can refer to squirrels of other genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Chipmunk_with_stuffed_cheeks_in_Prospect_Park_%2805980%29.jpg/330px-Chipmunk_with_stuffed_cheeks_in_Prospect_Park_%2805980%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chipmunk","wikidata":"Q18227870"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Chipmunk_with_stuffed_cheeks_in_Prospect_Park_%2805980%29.jpg/500px-Chipmunk_with_stuffed_cheeks_in_Prospect_Park_%2805980%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm